worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_capabilities_and_runtime_rules.js"
  ceiling 716
  rationale "Known-fact inventory queries, runtime rule updates, feature capability status, the architecture explanation and translation phrase normalization. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved to 1223 for issue #1175 R3 (follow-up round, 2026-10-08): the action-correction arm of the conversation-control twin records conversation_control:refusal when there is no earlier action to correct. Lowered to 1179 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the conversation-topic opener reader and its four-language prose left for the conversation_topic rule of data/seed/handler-rules.lino. Lowered to 929 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the feature-capability table and its yes, no, reason and web-search sentences moved to data/seed/feature-capabilities.lino and data/seed/multilingual-responses-capabilities.lino, read as the native handler reads them. Lowered to 925 the same day: architectureExplanationContent renders the seeded meta_explanation_architecture record instead of four inline sentences. Lowered from 925 to 704 on 2026-10-08 for R1188-U1: the capability listings became the seeded capabilities and capabilities_more responses, and the offline translation phrase table became translation_phrase meanings in data/seed/meanings-translation-phrases.lino, and the rule-detail openings the seeded rule_detail_request role. Ceiling moved 704 to 706 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds. Ceiling moved 706 to 716 for R1188-U19 (2026-10-09): roundTripSurface picks among the offered translation surfaces the one js/agentic/crate/round_trip_translation.mjs roundTripChoice finds survives the round trip, as Rust Translation::round_trip_surface does, and deformalizeMeaning answers with it."
